   "text": "```python\n\"\"\"\nlru_ttl_cache: A comprehensive, thread-safe LRU cache with Time-To-Live (TTL) expiry.\n\nThis module provides a robust implementation of a Least Recently Used (LRU) cache\nthat supports expiration of entries based on a Time-To-Live (TTL) mechanism.\nIt is designed to be thread-safe and suitable for multi-threaded applications.\n\nKey Features:\n    1. LRU Eviction: When the cache reaches its maximum size, the least recently\n       used item is evicted.\n    2. TTL Expiry: Entries expire after a specified duration, regardless of their\n       recency. Expired entries are automatically removed.\n    3. Thread Safety: All public methods are thread-safe.\n    4. Configuration: Supports configurable max size and default TTL.\n    5. Metrics: Tracks hit rates, eviction counts, and insertion counts.\n\nUsage Example:\n    from lru_ttl_cache import LRUTTLCache\n\n    cache = LRUTTLCache(max_size=100, default_ttl=3600)\n    cache.set('key', 'value', ttl=60)\n    value = cache.get('key')  # Returns 'value' if not expired and within TTL\n\n    # Accessing expired key\n    time.sleep(65)\n    value = cache.get('key')  # Returns None\n\nThread Safety:\n    The implementation uses a lock to ensure thread safety. In Python, the GIL\n    (Global Interpreter Lock) provides some level of atomicity, but for complex\n    operations involving multiple locks or external resources, explicit locking\n    is often necessary. This module uses `threading.Lock` for synchronization.\n\nPerformance Considerations:\n    - O(1) Average Time Complexity for get and set operations.\n    - O(n) Time Complexity for clear operation (where n is max_size).\n    - Memory usage is proportional to max_size.\n\nVersion: 1.0.0\nAuthor: AI Assistant\nDate: 2023\n\"\"\"\n\nimport threading\nimport time\nimport weakref\nfrom collections import OrderedDict\nfrom typing import Any, Callable, Dict, List, Optional, TypeVar, Generic, Union\nimport functools\nimport warnings\nimport sys\